{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SWJacksonMomentFactorization","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SWCoreJacobi"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.tendsto_jacksonLogCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.tendsto_jacksonLogCorrection","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TropicalClassTransport.lean#L114-L132","doc":"**The Jackson correction contributes nothing to the class in the\nlimit.** For `1 < q`, `log(1 − q^{-(k+1)}) → 0`; dividing by the fixed\n`log q̃` gives the `log_q̃`-error term of the tropical class, so the\nbalanced tropical class converges to `frac(log_q̃ E)` — the `u ≡ 1`\nclass — at a geometric rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.balancedNormalizer_ratio_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.balancedNormalizer_ratio_div","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TropicalClassTransport.lean#L101-L110","doc":"Quotient form of the transport: the balanced ratio equals the SW\nratio `v^k` times `E = 1/(1−p)` times the Jackson correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.balancedNormalizer_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.balancedNormalizer_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TropicalClassTransport.lean#L72-L99","doc":"**THE TRANSPORT (exact, division-free).** With `p = (v²)⁻¹` the\nbalanced normalizer's ratio is the SW ratio `v^k` scaled by `E = 1/(1−p)`\nand corrected by the Jackson factor `(1 − p^{k+1})`:\n\n    N^bal(k+2)·(1 − p) = N^bal(k+1)·v^k·(1 − p^{k+1}).\n\nDerived from the merged exact factorization; no perturbation argument,\nno asymptotics. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.swMoment_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TropicalClassTransport.swMoment_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TropicalClassTransport.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**The SW core's moment ratio is exactly `v^n`.** Since `v^n` is an\ninteger power of the lattice step, the core's tropical class is exactly\n`0` at every index — an exact statement, with no limit involved. ","signatureChunk":0}]}